From: fil-c-utils maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Reject years ctime cannot print under Fil-C

musl's asctime_r deliberately crashes when its ISO C format would not fit
the 26-byte buffer, which is any year outside -999..9999; under Fil-C that
is a null-pointer write panic that kills the server. glibc returns NULL
with EOVERFLOW for exactly those years, so #{t:...} expands to nothing;
check the local year first and do the same.

--- a/format.c
+++ b/format.c
@@ -4747,0 +4748,11 @@
+#ifdef __FILC__
+				/*
+				 * musl's asctime_r aborts if the result does
+				 * not fit in 26 bytes, so check the year it
+				 * would print first (glibc fails instead).
+				 */
+				if (localtime_r(&t, &tm) == NULL ||
+				    tm.tm_year < -999 - 1900 ||
+				    tm.tm_year > 9999 - 1900)
+					return (NULL);
+#endif
